<title>FRANCE: EU seen valuing early-Jan French wheat at $160.</title>
<headline>EU seen valuing early-Jan French wheat at $160.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>A European Union award of 397,500 tonnes of free-market soft wheat at a maximum refund of 11.94 Ecus per tonne values a tonne of early January French wheat at $159.87 per tonne, Reuters calculates.</p>
<p>The figure, which should be regarded as an estimate or a basis for rounding only, is calculated from standard-quality French milling wheat at Rouen and may vary significantly for other EU origins and types.</p>
</text>
